# StudyMate AI — Environment Configuration Overview
#
# StudyMate AI consists of two parts, each with its own .env file:
#
# 1. Backend (.env located in backend/):
#    Holds private credentials, Flask SECRET_KEY, database path, local Ollama/Gemma
#    configuration, and allowed CORS origins. Never expose these in frontend files.
#    See backend/.env.example for details.
#
# 2. Frontend (.env located in frontend/):
#    Holds public client-side configuration only (e.g., VITE_API_BASE_URL).
#    See frontend/.env.example for details.
#
# Setup Instructions for Offline Mode:
#   1. Copy backend/.env.example to backend/.env and verify Ollama settings.
#   2. Copy frontend/.env.example to frontend/.env.
#   3. Ensure Ollama is running (`ollama serve` and `ollama run gemma4:latest`).
#   4. Start Flask backend (port 5000): python app.py
#   5. Start React frontend (port 3000): npm run dev
